WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.152
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.422 --> 00:48.465
What's this?

3
00:48.548 --> 00:49.966
You're making a move on your own?

4
00:50.800 --> 00:52.510
-And who were you talking to? -My asset.

5
00:52.594 --> 00:53.845
And since when did you have an asset?

6
00:53.928 --> 00:56.097
Just leave me alone, Alex. I know what I'm doing.

7
00:56.723 --> 00:58.683
What matters is I can reach him through the landline,

8
00:58.767 --> 01:00.560
and he gives me vital information.

9
01:02.437 --> 01:04.731
Rahmboy, son, go with Chiara,

10
01:04.814 --> 01:07.067
so the Castellanis can see you.

11
01:12.822 --> 01:15.742
That's why the Moravianos don't take you seriously.

12
01:17.786 --> 01:19.079
Rahmboy, you're coming with me.

13
01:24.626 --> 01:28.254
Are you telling me, Mikoy, that you're getting all of this

14
01:28.338 --> 01:29.756
from your secret asset?

15
01:29.839 --> 01:31.466
-Yes, sir. -How do you know

16
01:31.549 --> 01:33.176
that your intel is legit?

17
01:33.259 --> 01:35.011
I'm sorry, my asset is top secret.

18
01:35.094 --> 01:36.763
Maybe in time, you'll understand why.

19
01:38.181 --> 01:40.809
She wants every move she makes to be a statement.

20
01:40.892 --> 01:43.269
She needs to prove through her actions

21
01:48.566 --> 01:49.943
We're on the same side.

22
01:50.026 --> 01:51.361
You can count on me, Chiara.

23
01:53.196 --> 01:54.989
But I want you to remember this too.

24
02:07.544 --> 02:11.089
Let's say Mikoy's intel is valid.

25
02:11.673 --> 02:14.509
The next question is, is it actionable?

26
02:15.802 --> 02:16.678
Exactly.

27
02:17.554 --> 02:19.848
Do you think Sir Norberto will agree?

28
02:19.931 --> 02:20.974
Didn't he

29
02:21.057 --> 02:22.725
say it himself

30
02:22.809 --> 02:24.435
that this is our golden window?

31
02:24.519 --> 02:27.856
If we don't act now and go to Italy right away,

32
02:27.939 --> 02:30.066
we'll end up wasting the intel we have.

33
02:30.150 --> 02:30.984
Exactly.

34
02:31.568 --> 02:34.821
Our golden window might just turn into a goodbye window.

35
02:36.614 --> 02:39.200
It is a golden window, theoretically speaking.

36
02:40.702 --> 02:41.870
But us,

37
02:41.953 --> 02:44.622
who is just a small intelligence agency from the Philippines

38
02:44.706 --> 02:47.458
who's already short on budget,

39
02:47.542 --> 02:48.960
what guarantee do we have

40
02:49.043 --> 02:51.796
that this mission will be successful?

41
02:52.338 --> 02:54.591
What guarantee do we have

42
02:54.674 --> 02:57.677
that we'll all make it back alive?

43
02:58.928 --> 03:00.722
Isn't that what every mission is like?

44
03:01.431 --> 03:03.433
There's always a risk involved.

45
03:04.100 --> 03:06.102
Half our lives are on the line.

46
03:07.896 --> 03:08.730
But it's okay.

47
03:08.813 --> 03:11.774
If you don't want to come with me, that's okay. I understand.

48
03:12.901 --> 03:14.903
Even just some moral support would be nice.

49
03:14.986 --> 03:15.945
That'll do.

50
03:16.029 --> 03:17.488
As for you, Mikoy,

51
03:17.572 --> 03:18.948
I have complete faith in you.

52
03:19.032 --> 03:20.366
Weren't you the one who taught me

53
03:20.450 --> 03:22.535
how to be a good person,

54
03:22.619 --> 03:24.120
how to do the right thing?

55
03:24.203 --> 03:25.204
Right?

56
03:25.830 --> 03:26.915
Mikoy.

57
03:32.462 --> 03:34.547
this isn't an ordinary mission.

58
03:35.215 --> 03:36.883
It's extremely dangerous.

59
03:38.134 --> 03:39.010
That's true.

60
03:40.053 --> 03:41.387
If you think about it,

61
03:41.471 --> 03:43.264
we're going to a place

62
03:43.348 --> 03:47.435
where the most powerful mafia are gathering for a meeting.

63
03:48.186 --> 03:50.271
We need to calculate every move we make.

64
03:51.272 --> 03:53.358
One mistake there,

65
03:54.400 --> 03:55.652
and we're all dead.

66
04:22.136 --> 04:25.014
I cannot let my mission fail.

67
05:01.634 --> 05:05.054
A black-and-white romcom is really your RRL for your research?

68
05:06.556 --> 05:08.016
A romcom, of all things.

69
05:08.933 --> 05:10.810
It's a classic for a reason.

70
05:11.519 --> 05:13.313
No matter how many times you watch it,

71
05:14.230 --> 05:15.815
it's still enjoyable.

72
05:17.734 --> 05:19.861
Is it still enjoyable if it doesn't have a happy ending?

73
05:19.944 --> 05:21.654
Oh, Mikoy.

74
05:21.738 --> 05:23.823
You really are a classic hopeless romantic.

75
05:26.159 --> 05:29.871
You know, we'd be better off talking about that over a few drinks.

76
05:48.306 --> 05:49.974
You're suddenly so quiet.

77
05:50.683 --> 05:52.435
You said earlier

78
05:52.518 --> 05:54.270
we'd talk about it over drinks.

79
05:58.357 --> 05:59.484
With or without alcohol,

80
05:59.567 --> 06:01.944
it's hard to talk about this mission, Mikoy.

81
06:06.657 --> 06:08.951
Mikoy, Chiara is our target.

82
06:14.082 --> 06:15.041
Really?

83
06:16.084 --> 06:17.752
Has it really come to this?

84
06:18.795 --> 06:20.588
We're actually ready to kill her?

85
06:28.012 --> 06:29.972
That's just how the world works.

86
06:31.724 --> 06:34.143
Maybe this really is the ending to our story.

87
06:36.187 --> 06:37.772
The person who used to be your ally,

88
06:38.564 --> 06:41.317
who stood beside you as you built your dreams for the future,

89
06:43.069 --> 06:45.488
you have to face her as if you never had a history together.

90
06:46.823 --> 06:48.533
Face her to make her pay.

91
06:49.534 --> 06:51.410
A life for a life.

92
06:59.127 --> 07:00.628
That's where you're wrong, Mikoy.

93
07:03.047 --> 07:04.590
No matter how you look at it, it's wrong.

94
07:04.674 --> 07:05.591
Why?

95
07:06.092 --> 07:07.885
Was it right when she killed my father?

96
07:14.308 --> 07:15.351
You said it yourself.

97
07:15.435 --> 07:17.103
Do it the right way.

98
07:17.770 --> 07:21.357
That's why I laid out my plan properly to the agencies, didn't I?

99
07:23.359 --> 07:26.154
Even if we say the agency supports this,

100
07:26.654 --> 07:28.531
even if there's an official order,

101
07:29.866 --> 07:31.200
it's still wrong.

102
07:36.080 --> 07:37.915
Because, Mikoy, this isn't you.

103
07:39.792 --> 07:42.670
You're not the kind of person who seeks revenge.

104
07:44.130 --> 07:46.799
And you're not the kind of person who can kill.

105
07:47.592 --> 07:49.594
Especially not the person you love most.

106
07:59.187 --> 08:00.813
The person I used to love.

107
08:09.322 --> 08:11.657
Love doesn't just disappear.

108
08:13.659 --> 08:15.203
Maybe some things just changed.

109
08:16.829 --> 08:18.789
Maybe it gained some layers

110
08:19.540 --> 08:21.209
or lost some of its intensity.

111
08:26.631 --> 08:28.090
Is that you, Alex?

112
08:28.174 --> 08:30.301
You're a hopeless romantic after all.

113
08:31.302 --> 08:34.680
I remember all those warnings you gave me about Chiara.

114
08:34.764 --> 08:36.182
You were so harsh back then.

115
08:39.727 --> 08:40.895
I was naive back then.

116
08:42.063 --> 08:44.065
I was blind to all those red flags.

117
08:45.608 --> 08:48.486
I always gave her the benefit of the doubt.

118
08:50.363 --> 08:52.490
Apparently, that's what happens when you're a romantic.

119
08:53.991 --> 08:55.451
You're always hopeful.

120
08:58.329 --> 08:59.705
Hopeful that

121
09:01.499 --> 09:03.000
things might still change.

122
09:05.336 --> 09:06.629
Hopeful that…

123
09:09.340 --> 09:11.133
there's still a tomorrow to look forward to.

124
09:12.969 --> 09:15.263
Maybe that's why it bothers me to see you like this.

125
09:19.976 --> 09:21.269
You're just not used to it.

126
09:22.937 --> 09:24.313
Everyone changes.

127
09:28.276 --> 09:30.444
I hope this mission can change you back.

128
09:33.489 --> 09:34.949
As much as my brain can't imagine

129
09:35.032 --> 09:37.535
you and Chiara getting back together, but you know,

130
09:38.411 --> 09:39.787
in my heart…

131
09:48.546 --> 09:51.215
Because I know you're just caught in a situation

132
09:52.550 --> 09:54.760
by the past you share that you can't escape.

133
10:00.641 --> 10:01.892
You know,

134
10:03.603 --> 10:05.438
I think you're drunk already, Alex.

135
10:07.064 --> 10:08.399
That's enough.

136
10:10.651 --> 10:12.028
Chiara and I are over,

137
10:12.903 --> 10:14.822
and there's nothing left to go back to.

138
10:16.574 --> 10:18.326
We've both chosen our own lives.

139
10:18.409 --> 10:20.077
For now, this is mine,

140
10:20.161 --> 10:21.829
to finish this mission.

141
10:21.912 --> 10:23.164
That's it.

142
10:26.542 --> 10:27.918
If that's the case…

143
10:29.962 --> 10:32.632
then I hope the old Mikoy I knew comes back.

144
10:37.136 --> 10:38.471
Even just that.

145
10:51.776 --> 10:53.986
let's just wait and see how this ends.

146
11:11.504 --> 11:12.671
Mom.

147
11:12.755 --> 11:15.091
You've been staring into space for a while now.

148
11:15.174 --> 11:17.593
Come eat. The food's getting cold.

149
11:20.429 --> 11:22.681
I was just thinking about your brother.

150
11:23.766 --> 11:25.684
I wonder how he's doing over there.

151
11:26.560 --> 11:28.479
He's always in Manila now,

152
11:28.562 --> 11:30.147
and he always seems so busy.

153
11:30.856 --> 11:32.858
I wonder what he's busy with now.

154
11:35.027 --> 11:37.446
He said he's okay, Mom.

155
11:38.072 --> 11:39.907
But we know him so well.

156
11:39.990 --> 11:43.160
He wouldn't admit it if he was having a hard time.

157
11:43.244 --> 11:46.038
He'll show that he can handle it,

158
11:46.122 --> 11:47.748
but deep down,

159
11:47.832 --> 11:49.458
he's struggling too.

160
11:52.002 --> 11:53.796
That's just how your brother is.

161
11:54.880 --> 11:56.090
But you know,

162
11:57.133 --> 11:59.718
no matter how heavy the burden is,

163
12:00.302 --> 12:02.972
I'm sure he'll get through all of it.

164
12:04.265 --> 12:05.850
You're right, Mom.

165
12:06.851 --> 12:08.185
But you know, Mom,

166
12:08.853 --> 12:12.690
if he keeps dealing with all his problems on his own,

167
12:12.773 --> 12:15.568
why don't we show him that we're here for him,

168
12:15.651 --> 12:16.819
that we support him,

169
12:16.902 --> 12:18.946
that we're his number one support system?

170
12:19.947 --> 12:20.781
Right?

171
12:20.865 --> 12:22.658
I agree with you, son.

172
12:25.244 --> 12:26.328
I have an idea.

173
12:32.710 --> 12:34.503
Hello, Captain Pepe.

174
12:35.004 --> 12:36.964
I was hoping to ask you a favor.

175
13:03.157 --> 13:04.867
It's so nice here!

176
13:07.578 --> 13:08.454
It's so cold here.

177
13:08.537 --> 13:09.580
It's so soft.

178
13:10.372 --> 13:11.499
Air-conditioning!

179
13:11.582 --> 13:13.334
-It's so soft! -Leather!

180
13:13.417 --> 13:14.335
Air-conditioning!

181
13:14.418 --> 13:16.253
What is wrong with you guys?

182
13:16.337 --> 13:18.797
What's with all these surprises?

183
13:19.632 --> 13:23.135
Because you're never online anymore on IG or Twitter.

184
13:23.219 --> 13:25.262
And you don't message in the group chat.

185
13:25.346 --> 13:27.765
You don't even view our My Days anymore.

186
13:27.848 --> 13:30.267
Don't you know they expire after 24 hours?

187
13:30.351 --> 13:31.685
Seriously!

188
13:31.769 --> 13:35.064
I can't even tell if you're my friends or my clingy girlfriends!

189
13:36.106 --> 13:37.358
Of course, Mikoy.

190
13:37.441 --> 13:39.360
We're a team. We're like the GILAS, right?

191
13:39.443 --> 13:40.528
When there's Mikoy…

192
13:40.611 --> 13:42.488
There's the Kolokoys!

193
13:43.072 --> 13:44.490
Heart!

194
13:44.573 --> 13:47.034
Mikoy, we miss you!

195
13:47.117 --> 13:47.952
Exactly.

196
13:51.747 --> 13:53.040
See?

197
13:53.123 --> 13:57.086
Even me, Mikoy, you take forever to reply.

198
13:57.169 --> 13:58.420
Even me, son.

199
13:58.504 --> 14:00.297
You don't answer my calls.

200
14:00.381 --> 14:01.215
See?

201
14:01.298 --> 14:02.633
See? See?

202
14:03.676 --> 14:05.094
I'm sorry, everyone.

203
14:05.719 --> 14:06.971
I've just been really busy.

204
14:07.054 --> 14:08.973
I've had a lot to take care of.

205
14:09.056 --> 14:11.225
What are you so busy with?

206
14:15.062 --> 14:16.605
It's a secret for now, Mom.

207
14:17.273 --> 14:19.400
Oh, here we go again, son.

208
14:19.483 --> 14:21.068
Another secret.

209
14:21.151 --> 14:22.152
Another secret.

210
14:22.236 --> 14:24.488
Is there something we should be worried about again, bro?

211
14:25.406 --> 14:27.741
No! I'm okay, okay?

212
14:27.825 --> 14:29.869
Guys, I'm really okay.

213
14:29.952 --> 14:31.787
I'm more than alright, actually.

214
14:31.871 --> 14:32.955
Are you sure?

215
14:33.038 --> 14:34.999
Yeah, but

216
14:35.082 --> 14:36.500
when the time is right,

217
14:36.584 --> 14:37.710
you'll all find out.

218
14:40.004 --> 14:42.006
For now, how about

219
14:42.756 --> 14:43.757
some ramyeon?

220
14:44.466 --> 14:45.301
Me!

221
14:45.384 --> 14:46.844
There's a good place nearby.

222
14:49.013 --> 14:50.764
-Okay! -Does it come with soup?

223
14:50.848 --> 14:52.433
-Of course! -No vegetables, right?

224
14:52.516 --> 14:54.476
Everything's for you guys!

225
14:54.560 --> 14:55.477
-Does it have soup? -Of course!

226
14:55.561 --> 14:57.062
No vegetables, right? No vegetables?

227
14:59.148 --> 15:02.610
Son, isn't it nice that the weather's so good today?

228
15:02.693 --> 15:03.694
The sun's out.

229
15:03.777 --> 15:05.237
Here in Manila,

230
15:05.321 --> 15:08.240
just a little rain and it floods!

231
15:09.158 --> 15:11.285
It's the same in some provinces, Mom.

232
15:11.368 --> 15:13.162
Climate change

233
15:13.245 --> 15:15.539
and all that corruption are really a bad combo.

234
15:15.623 --> 15:16.707
You said it!

235
15:16.790 --> 15:18.584
And people who just throw their trash everywhere!

236
15:18.667 --> 15:19.877
You know what needs to happen?

237
15:19.960 --> 15:22.546
Those officials need to be held accountable,

238
15:22.630 --> 15:25.174
and those corrupt people need to go to jail!

239
15:25.257 --> 15:26.175
-Exactly! -Exactly!

240
15:26.258 --> 15:28.135
Anyone involved with them should go to jail too!

241
15:28.218 --> 15:29.678
-Absolutely! -Exactly!

242
15:30.179 --> 15:31.597
Even my pancit is overflowing,

243
15:31.680 --> 15:33.599
drowning in soup!

244
15:33.682 --> 15:35.017
This is so good!

245
15:35.684 --> 15:36.769
Wait a minute, son.

246
15:36.852 --> 15:39.355
Do I mix in this seasoning now?

247
15:40.814 --> 15:41.774
Oh, wait!

248
16:04.129 --> 16:05.631
Just relax, Chiara!

249
16:06.256 --> 16:09.551
It's instant cooking. It'll be ready in a bit!

250
16:09.635 --> 16:10.678
Oh, you.

251
16:10.761 --> 16:12.471
Sweetheart, what are you doing?

252
16:12.554 --> 16:15.516
They say if you lift the noodles a little

253
16:16.892 --> 16:18.519
it lets air in,

254
16:18.602 --> 16:20.396
and it'll make the noodles firmer.

255
16:21.855 --> 16:22.982
Really?

256
16:23.482 --> 16:24.525
It seems like the same thing to me.

257
16:24.608 --> 16:26.026
They're going to cook anyway!

258
16:40.624 --> 16:41.667
Nice!

259
16:42.167 --> 16:43.377
You're really good, sweetheart!

260
16:43.460 --> 16:44.670
Look!

261
16:44.753 --> 16:46.505
The noodles are cooked perfectly!

262
16:46.588 --> 16:49.717
And it looks like the seasoning stuck better!

263
17:02.855 --> 17:04.189
So, Mikoy?

264
17:05.065 --> 17:06.900
How was your flashback?

265
17:17.828 --> 17:19.580
Wasn't it such a happy time back then,

266
17:20.164 --> 17:21.623
when you two were still okay?

267
17:24.710 --> 17:26.879
It's hard when you're trying to move on

268
17:26.962 --> 17:29.089
and happy memories suddenly come flooding back.

269
17:30.758 --> 17:32.551
Will you two stop it? Stop!

270
17:32.634 --> 17:34.762
Seriously, just leave Brother Mikoy alone for now.

271
17:34.845 --> 17:37.514
Everyone who's been heartbroken and is trying to move on

272
17:37.598 --> 17:40.309
has to go through it. You can't rush the process.

273
17:42.770 --> 17:44.438
You're one to talk about rushing.

274
17:45.939 --> 17:47.524
You all, really.

275
17:47.608 --> 17:48.984
Eat up.

276
17:49.068 --> 17:50.277
It's still hot.

277
17:51.320 --> 17:52.404
Bro Mikoy.

278
17:53.447 --> 17:55.240
What stage are you at now?

279
17:58.410 --> 17:59.787
-Hangry stage? -I'm starving.

280
17:59.870 --> 18:01.914
Then eat it already.

281
18:01.997 --> 18:02.998
There you go.

282
18:03.082 --> 18:04.124
I'm going to eat it.

283
18:05.584 --> 18:06.794
Come on, Mom. Eat up.

284
18:36.573 --> 18:37.950
What's wrong, dear?

285
18:40.202 --> 18:41.787
Do you miss Mikoy?

286
18:43.330 --> 18:44.331
Or

287
18:45.082 --> 18:47.960
do you miss the Philippines?

288
18:53.590 --> 18:55.300
Have some ramyeon first.

289
18:55.384 --> 18:58.929
Maybe it'll help you miss the Philippines a little less.

290
19:01.181 --> 19:02.891
That's Korean noodles.

291
19:04.351 --> 19:05.644
Exactly.

292
19:06.436 --> 19:08.772
But it's really popular in the Philippines.

293
19:09.439 --> 19:11.024
You know Filipinos.

294
19:11.108 --> 19:13.527
We never want to miss out on a trend.

295
19:16.905 --> 19:17.990
Dear.

296
19:18.073 --> 19:19.992
I understand what you're going through.

297
19:21.034 --> 19:23.287
I know this isn't easy for you.

298
19:23.370 --> 19:25.038
But we're almost there.

299
19:25.873 --> 19:27.374
Just hang in there a little longer.

300
19:28.542 --> 19:32.296
We'll sort out our problems with the Castellanis.

301
19:33.297 --> 19:36.049
We'll all be able to breathe easier.

302
19:39.303 --> 19:41.805
That sounds impossible, Mama Yaya.

303
19:44.266 --> 19:48.228
In the mafia life, there's always one problem after another,

304
19:48.312 --> 19:50.063
big or small.

305
19:50.939 --> 19:53.859
Even if we manage to settle things with the Castellanis,

306
19:54.443 --> 19:56.653
I'm sure there'll be another one

307
19:56.737 --> 19:59.656
that'll challenge my leadership of the Concordat.

308
20:01.700 --> 20:02.910
Look at me.

309
20:04.578 --> 20:08.498
La Morte Bianca raised me and trained me.

310
20:08.582 --> 20:09.708
But

311
20:10.751 --> 20:13.212
I still managed to stand up against her.

312
20:16.673 --> 20:18.133
I know, dear.

313
20:20.427 --> 20:22.012
That's why I'm here,

314
20:22.596 --> 20:24.473
always supporting you.

315
20:26.391 --> 20:28.477
Whatever you need,

316
20:28.560 --> 20:31.480
I'm ready to give it to you.

317
20:32.481 --> 20:33.982
For now,

318
20:34.066 --> 20:37.194
let's focus on the Castellanis.

319
20:38.362 --> 20:40.614
We know how cunning they are.

320
20:41.365 --> 20:43.075
So let's be careful.

321
20:50.958 --> 20:52.334
Mikoy.

322
20:53.210 --> 20:55.295
Tell me the truth.

323
20:56.546 --> 20:58.006
How are you?

324
20:58.590 --> 21:01.343
What have you been so busy with, son?

325
21:02.302 --> 21:03.512
And hold on.

326
21:03.595 --> 21:06.974
Don't give me some showbiz-style answer and dodge the question.

327
21:07.516 --> 21:10.185
You can't just keep denying everything.

328
21:12.604 --> 21:15.065
I saw your gun earlier.

329
21:17.484 --> 21:18.944
I'm your mother.

330
21:19.027 --> 21:21.113
I deserve to know the truth.

331
21:27.703 --> 21:28.745
Mom,

332
21:29.830 --> 21:31.832
I've returned to active duty with the agency.

333
21:35.794 --> 21:36.962
Since when?

334
21:38.005 --> 21:40.424
Is that why you're always here in Manila?

335
21:42.801 --> 21:44.136
Yes, Mom.

336
21:44.761 --> 21:46.430
And we have a mission.

337
21:54.229 --> 21:56.606
That's exactly what I was afraid of.

338
21:57.441 --> 22:00.235
Son, why did you have to go back to that agency?

339
22:00.319 --> 22:03.572
You know there's no guarantee with those missions.

340
22:07.075 --> 22:08.994
And after this mission,

341
22:09.077 --> 22:11.747
I'm really going back to a quiet, simple life.

342
22:13.081 --> 22:14.166
I promise you that.

343
22:16.209 --> 22:17.627
Oh, son.

344
22:17.711 --> 22:20.464
Nothing good ever comes from those missions!

345
22:20.547 --> 22:22.841
We just lost your father.

346
22:22.924 --> 22:26.428
You're all I have left. You and Angelito.

347
22:27.137 --> 22:28.638
I'll be careful, Mom.

348
22:30.515 --> 22:32.184
Mom, I'm really sorry.

349
22:32.809 --> 22:34.186
But I have to do this.

350
22:35.145 --> 22:37.397
Mom, I have to do this for Dad.

351
22:38.774 --> 22:40.067
For Mario?

352
22:40.901 --> 22:43.653
You're going to avenge your father?

353
22:44.780 --> 22:47.157
Revenge isn't the answer, son.

354
22:48.742 --> 22:51.495
Mom, I understand that you're worried about me.

355
22:52.454 --> 22:53.455
But, Mom,

356
22:54.623 --> 22:56.249
I've already made my decision.

357
22:57.375 --> 22:59.544
And I'm fully committed to this mission.

358
23:01.004 --> 23:01.963
Mikoy.

359
23:02.923 --> 23:04.800
You know, I know

360
23:04.883 --> 23:07.219
how heavy the burden you're carrying is.

361
23:07.803 --> 23:09.387
Okay, I know that.

362
23:10.222 --> 23:14.017
But revenge isn't the answer, son.

363
23:14.101 --> 23:16.103
I know you.

364
23:17.729 --> 23:20.232
I know you have a good heart,

365
23:20.315 --> 23:23.443
and no matter how much anger and pain you're going through,

366
23:23.527 --> 23:25.320
I know you'll make the right decision

367
23:25.403 --> 23:27.489
because you're a good person, son.

368
23:28.323 --> 23:30.242
You have a good heart.

369
23:46.091 --> 23:48.343
I called Malacañang last night.

370
23:48.426 --> 23:51.304
The Office of the President had already given its approval.

371
24:05.610 --> 24:06.653
-Okay… -Excuse me.

372
24:06.736 --> 24:07.988
-Excuse me. -Hey!

373
24:33.847 --> 24:35.765
to everyone entering and leaving the restaurant,

374
24:35.849 --> 24:38.310
and all I need is one shot to take her out.

375
24:38.393 --> 24:39.644
And what will Mikoy do?

376
24:47.319 --> 24:50.822
They call us criminals, a syndicate.

377
24:50.906 --> 24:52.324
But aren't they the ones

378
24:53.241 --> 24:55.493
who are actually the syndicate and criminals?

379
24:57.204 --> 25:00.207
I hope your wish is

380
25:00.290 --> 25:03.627
that everything goes smoothly tomorrow.

381
25:14.221 --> 25:16.389
I gave my heart to the wrong person.

382
25:16.473 --> 25:19.226
But please, Mikoy, continue believing in love.

383
25:19.309 --> 25:21.353
Despite the world not believing in it.
